From fe764cb8a0ac92516b72ecfb66704e1909cd35fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:34:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 188/209] fix(audio): area components do not move their own
 host entity

CEntityComponentAudio and the CryDefaultEntities audio CAreaComponent both
move THEIR OWN entity in response to area events: OnListenerEnter,
OnListenerMoveNear, OnListenerMoveInside and OnListenerExclusiveMoveInside
call m_pEntity->SetPos(), and the modern component does the same at six
places in its ProcessEvent. That is correct while the audio emitter and the
area live on two different, linked entities, which is the only arrangement
legacy content produces - CArea::AddEntity is never called with the area's
own entity there.

It is a feedback loop as soon as one entity hosts both: moving the entity
moves the area with it, the area produces a new near event, which moves the
entity again. A component that hosts its own area and attaches itself to it
(the BoidsProxy pattern) hits this immediately, and so does the Area function
component of CryPlugins/AreaComponents, whose whole point is that these two
audio components keep working unmodified on the same entity.

Guard both with the cheapest correct test: all six CArea events carry the
area's HOST entity in nParam[2] (for MOVEINSIDEAREA the low area, with the
high one in nParam[3]), so comparing it against the component's own entity id
costs one integer compare - no entity lookup, no walk of the area's attached
list. Only the SetPos() calls are skipped; state, fade values and every
Schematyc signal are unaffected.

Behaviour for existing content is unchanged: the two ids are never equal
there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
